<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Privacy-preserving device health (Issue #24).

    Kept in its own file rather than appended to strings.xml so the health report
    owns its vocabulary. Android merges every values/*.xml into one resource
    table, so keys must still be globally unique; they all carry the `health_`
    prefix for that reason.

    Every key here must also exist in res/values-iw/device_health_strings.xml.
    DeviceHealthStringsParityTest.java enforces that, including format
    placeholders, and it also ties this file to the enums in
    DeviceHealthAssessor and DeviceHealthSnapshot: a finding, a status, a
    severity or a state added in code without a sentence here fails the build.
-->
